  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+2}$ in the form $x=\\theta +n\\cdot b$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{180}^{\u2218}),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in degrees.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that $tan\\,({75}^{\u2218})=\\sqrt{3}+2.$*\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =\\sqrt{3}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\sqrt{3}+2)={75}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{\u2218}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={75}^{\u2218}+n\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
